<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Jensen Huang’s return has calmed markets but fears of an AI bubble still run deep</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc6c4265c7773a62aa67bca893fda7e55e0c6d8dc5e54a09c222b38d7fb8e482</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T07:15:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-jensen-huang-s-return-has-calmed-markets-but-fears-of-an-ai-bubble-still-run-deep--4522ba2897b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-jensen-huang-s-return-has-calmed-markets-but-fears-of-an-ai-bubble-still-run-deep" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's decision to bring back Jensen Huang as CEO pushed the AI computing company's stocks up more than 30 percent Monday. But the model of circular financing increasingly underwriting the AI boom still has some analysts worried that the party can't last forever.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US flew surveillance drone over Mexico to help capture top drug lord</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eff2fa21ced12bc86183e40eae399837a60445d141d2cb01cdbdba6aa4a687e9</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T02:09:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-us-flew-surveillance-drone-over-mexico-to-help-capture-top-drug-lord--342d551a758c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-us-flew-surveillance-drone-over-mexico-to-help-capture-top-drug-lord" /><summary type="html">Mexican officials say the United States flew a surveillance drone over Mexican territory to help locate and capture one of the country's most wanted drug traffickers. The operation led to the arrest of Fausto Isidro Meza Flores, known as 'El Chapo Isidro'.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump backs Nvidia boss's return but top Democrat vows probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac7c07661352c7c65250c29f191a8fbbd922b5e24013cb97a8c4a0e79a889db4</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:53:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-backs-nvidia-boss-s-return-but-top-democrat-vows-probe--0b7b3a362597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-backs-nvidia-boss-s-return-but-top-democrat-vows-probe" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump praised Nvidia's decision Monday to reinstate Jensen Huang as chief executive, as top Senate Democrat Chuck Schumer vowed to investigate potential wrongdoing amid mounting national security concerns. Trump also posted a doctored version of the famous photograph of him raising his fist after surviving a 2024 assassination attempt, replacing himself with Huang, who brandished a red bra beneath an Nvidia flag. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Maintain control': UN chief calls for creation of global AI safety framework within a year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48050c1445b8732b817836aeb1c3a4b21da6093354e4b2104bb95882b88ea2fe</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:06:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-un-chief-antonio-guterres-calls-for-global-ai-safety-framework-within-a-year--b8cbcdfbe9c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-un-chief-antonio-guterres-calls-for-global-ai-safety-framework-within-a-year" /><summary type="html">UN chief Antonio Guterres on Monday urged countries to agree on the creation of a global framework for managing the dangers posed by artificial intelligence within one year. Speaking at a summit in Barbados, he warned that taming the technology is vital if humanity is to stay in charge of its own future.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats vow probe after Trump forces Huang's return as Nvidia CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff2efe1108f68f6f5da02e67e3c12e6b8266367b97b594ba83a8c8c421231b94</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:06:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says--1a69aac9014a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-nvidia-board-reinstates-disgraced-jensen-huang-as-ceo-president-says" /><summary type="html">Nvidia on ⁠Monday said it ​was immediately reinstating disgraced tech titan Jensen Huang as its chief executive, marking an extraordinary reversal ​under pressure from US President Donald Trump, who said he had directly intervened within Nvidia's board. Democratic Senate leader Chuck Schumer vowed to investigate potential wrongdoing by "anybody selling out our national security for financial gain".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Out of control': ICE agents make arrests at Seattle airport in 'horrific' scene</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:088436683c969b120cdce57d2565e14df0176b82ab3986e602e9c60f1b4a1e3f</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T12:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-out-of-control-ice-agents-make-arrests-at-seattle-airport-in-horrific-scene--3d2cfac9c9ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-out-of-control-ice-agents-make-arrests-at-seattle-airport-in-horrific-scene" /><summary type="html">The governor of Washington state called US federal immigration agents "out of control" after they arrested two people at Seattle's main airport on Saturday. ICE officers have conducted raids across the United States, part of President Donald Trump's immigration crackdown which has forged ahead despite a rebuke by voters at this month's midterms.</summary></entry><entry><title>Alice Huang had contact with China spy agency during affair with Nvidia boss, New York Times reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5baef55543b9feedbe6882787a65a83bf17182aee92d22fdf98a1291e26b40a6</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:48:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-alice-huang-had-contact-with-china-spy-agency-during-affair-with-nvidia-boss-nyt-reports--c1a1f982d978.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261123-alice-huang-had-contact-with-china-spy-agency-during-affair-with-nvidia-boss-nyt-reports" /><summary type="html">Alice Huang, who is alleged to have been spying for Chinese intelligence during her affair with former Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, was in contact with China's Ministry of State Security until autumn 2026, the New York Times reported Monday, citing people with knowledge of US intelligence reports.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Democrat Hubbard wins North Carolina recount, clinching historic House majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93e11207c77bacb58e323998add3beffe9c71eee7d151fe9a1becd5ed8ee1c2d</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T20:16:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority--58e941bd0d61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261122-democrat-hubbard-wins-north-carolina-recount-clinching-historic-house-majority" /><summary type="html">Democrat Chuck Hubbard was elected to the US House of Representatives from North Carolina on Sunday after defeating veteran Republican Virginia Foxx, who chairs the powerful House Rules Committee. His victory gave Democrats their best general election result in decades, winning at least 258 seats in the 2026 US midterms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>FBI criminal database hacked</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543247ea107e5aebadb4b64a91df3d382af7410ac970920343e58c3b371104a7</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:23:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fbi-criminal-database-hacked--0e998fd7b8f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fbi-criminal-database-hacked" /><summary type="html">The FBI is investigating a reported major cyberattack targeting its national law enforcement database, the National Crime Information Center (NCIC), which holds sensitive criminal justice records, including information on fugitives, missing persons, criminal histories and stolen property. President Donald Trump said he had just been briefed on the incident, describing it as “not good”. FRANCE 24’s Fraser Jackson reports from Washington DC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Man convicted of starting palisades fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f264c4544ade5ad44b66258df41dd0f5c67ae6bfe17351646cf681d09f56df0</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T17:21:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/man-convicted-of-starting-palisades-fire--96bd39830bc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/man-convicted-of-starting-palisades-fire" /><summary type="html">A Los Angeles County jury found former rideshare driver Jonathan Rinderknecht guilty on Friday of starting the 2025 Palisades fire, which caused widespread destruction and loss of life. He faces a prison sentence of between five and 40 years. Liza Kaminov has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mexico captures drug cartel boss ‘El Chapo Isidro’ after deadly firefight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29eb6231c036d8462750f6cddb51c064b6fcf033b946871e0509d9fed5841546</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:00:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-mexico-captures-drug-cartel-boss-el-chapo-isidro-after-deadly-firefight--4de2de04ed1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-mexico-captures-drug-cartel-boss-el-chapo-isidro-after-deadly-firefight" /><summary type="html">Mexico's military forces captured ​one of the most wanted suspected drug lords, Fausto Isidro Meza Flores, known as "El Chapo Isidro," the military announced on Saturday, after a deadly firefight that killed seven suspected attackers and four soldiers. Flores, one of the FBI’s 10 most wanted fugitives, was flown to Mexico City after his capture.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Agriculture Department and FBI hit by cyberattacks, media report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b8ab1c85a636c8f25aaa4f71932e61e4cc5cd47974deb51d71311025b291c14</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T07:01:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-us-agriculture-department-fbi-hit-by-cyberattacks-media-report--56cdf33f7140.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-us-agriculture-department-fbi-hit-by-cyberattacks-media-report" /><summary type="html">Hackers breached systerms at the US Agriculture Department and the FBI, US media reported, amid a recent wave of major technology disruptions across the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>House of Cards: America's enemies 'no longer fear it, its allies no longer trust it'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98723359d18259a91efae087fd1633306e55375044a0c6b766e011e2790c3220</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T22:13:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-house-of-cards-america-s-enemies-no-longer-fear-it-its-allies-no-longer-trust-it--88bb89bac749.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-house-of-cards-america-s-enemies-no-longer-fear-it-its-allies-no-longer-trust-it" /><summary type="html">The Economist's Deputy editor Tom Standage joins us for a futuristic retrospective, taking us back to the future as we spotlight "The World Ahead 2027". We begin with the "leader of the free world", US President Donald Trump, presiding over an America under the "Donroe Doctrine". For Standage, America's "enemies no longer fear it and its allies no longer trust it in the way they did before."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>🦛 USA: Fiona, Cincinnati Zoo’s famous hippo, has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ea0e5d5c61b06e2af24159d41f6b887bd2c9b1ab6142e69b8101a904cd2f4c8</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:35:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-_-usa-fiona-cincinnati-zoo-s-famous-hippo-has-died--6b77bb696bc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-%F0%9F%A6%9B-usa-fiona-cincinnati-zoo-s-famous-hippo-has-died" /><summary type="html">🦛Fiona, Cincinnati Zoo’s beloved hippo, has died aged just 9, after swallowing a knitted hat that fell into her enclosure. Born prematurely and weighing only 13kg, she captured millions of hearts around the world and became an internet sensation.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump hails 'fantastic' relationships with China's Xi, Russia's Putin after three-way talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f09b6e0d252c69af3b24011c853ac1edf2dd87b70075af44e5a11adefc802070</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin--de6586fb5a55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-watch-live-trump-holds-press-conference-meeting-xi-putin" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump played up his "fantastic" relationships with China's Xi Jinping and Russia's Vladimir Putin during a White House press conference on Friday following his return to Washington after a first-ever trilateral meeting with the Chinese and Russian leaders. Here are key takeaways from his wide-ranging briefing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Jamaica's beaches are increasingly off limits to locals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e64873b27d588c9db584014178c65f6224baba3b94329665678cfa0b7c14f2b</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:55:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels--8b1ba04df6ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261120-jamaica-beaches-off-limits-to-locals-property-developers-hotels" /><summary type="html">Jamaica usually conjures up images of white sandy beaches, Rastafari culture and Bob Marley – but another reality exists. On this small Caribbean island, less than 1 percent of the coastline is freely accessible to local people. The rest has gradually been privatised, mostly for large hotel developments and private homes.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador: Nayib Bukele, self-proclaimed “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7dc638fc57c038a932d573cee526a669f6b74fc90629e8dbdd625340b5bb019c</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:07:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term--1aebd0b55990.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/el-salvador-nayib-bukele-self-proclaimed-coolest-dictator-on-earth-is-seeking-a-third-term" /><summary type="html">🇸🇻 El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele, who calls himself the “coolest dictator on earth”, is seeking a third term after changing the Constitution to scrap presidential term limits. His war on gangs has made him hugely popular, but also sparked serious human rights concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>White House fires national cyber director over widespread outages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6387e2e253960dbd4c5dd2cb01a331d7d8981111a4fd18502e429984a9bc9c93</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T01:28:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-white-house-fires-national-cyber-director-over-widespread-outages--e5d5af4d4476.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261120-white-house-fires-national-cyber-director-over-widespread-outages" /><summary type="html">The White House fired national cyber director Sean Cairncross on Thursday following a week of technology disruptions affecting US air travel, email services and national security systems. The departure comes as the Trump administration faces criticism over its response to the outages, which officials say were unrelated incidents.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Armed forces in Haiti kill at least 34 gang members to regain control of key corridor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed7d7a37da62a920f87904d7a0b4abfa7193fada934a4fbbf92b9a22902b2e8d</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T22:31:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261119-major-anti-gang-offensive-in-haiti-kills-34-suspected-gang-members--26a4355e6e18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261119-major-anti-gang-offensive-in-haiti-kills-34-suspected-gang-members" /><summary type="html">Haitian security forces launched a major offensive on Thursday to retake Martissant, a strategic corridor linking Port-au-Prince with the country's western and southern regions that gangs have controlled for five years. Police said at least 34 suspected gang members were killed in clashes involving a private security task force.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>A president among body bags: Photo ops spark outrage in Colombia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19dc3c09d9d7a6ba32dd635620726ee6c8e69c71ed21c80c00c27055c9e378c2</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:52:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261119-president-body-bags-photo-ops-sparking-outrage-colombia--7fdcc25cb912.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261119-president-body-bags-photo-ops-sparking-outrage-colombia" /><summary type="html">Since taking office in August, Colombia's far-right President Abelardo de la Espriella has regularly posted videos that show him walking among body bags supposedly holding the remains of rebel fighters – a communications strategy that has sparked widespread criticism.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Voyager 1 phones home from record one light-day away, 49 years after launch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:714cd6db5955704531a871897790fa9989fc5f510fe813f4c3714829be54f8d0</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nasa-voyager-1-phones-home-from-record-one-light-day-away-49-years-after-launch--ea85baca7960.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nasa-voyager-1-phones-home-from-record-one-light-day-away-49-years-after-launch" /><summary type="html">The Voyager 1 probe launched by NASA nearly a half century ago has reached a distance from Earth of one light day (more than 26 billion kilometres), the farthest any human artifact has ever ventured from our planet. The space agency received a signal from the spacecraft Thursday, exactly 24 hours after it was sent.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Xi, Putin summit: What was it all about?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38bf090f5361b3291ff4e8ed32ce51ec6f29f612e5469c6e06a6522c5877f8be</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:12:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-xi-putin-summit-what-was-it-all-about--2c0baba62b07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-xi-putin-summit-what-was-it-all-about" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has left China after a historic first meeting with Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Ukraine was discussed without Kyiv or European leaders in the room, which raised eyebrows, though Trump defended dialogue with rivals and Putin said the talks created conditions for future agreements. Xi warned major powers against conflict, and topics included reducing nuclear risks, reforming the UN and increasing energy flows.</summary></entry><entry><title>Haiti: Salvador’s Bukele publishes video of attack on gang leader’s house</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed2dd89f51c21b51eb153a60ec558a603cc17d5be93c587f509217175afb0d4</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:06:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-haiti-salvador-s-bukele-publishes-video-of-attack-on-gang-leader-s-house--14ac3f8f83f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-haiti-salvador-s-bukele-publishes-video-of-attack-on-gang-leader-s-house" /><summary type="html">Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele said Wednesday that his troops demolished the lavish home of a prominent gang leader in Haiti known as Jeff Gwo Lwa. "My gift to the Haitian people on the anniversary of the Battle of Vertières," Bukele wrote on X - referencing a 1803 battle critical in helping secure Haiti's independence from France.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Democrats nominate Jeffries to be first Black House speaker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9b59ea08d0428d33184f4df9c6982d85682c373a63a4015511f536656511b50</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:58:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker--1a82a2206b26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-democrats-nominate-jeffries-to-be-first-black-house-speaker" /><summary type="html">Hakeem Jeffries is on the cusp of becoming the first Black speaker of the US House of Representatives after Democrats elected him their leader Wednesday following a sweeping midterm election triumph. Jeffries faced no declared challenger, although opposition from some newly elected progressives had exposed divisions over how Democrats should wield their newfound power. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hegseth makes surprise trip to Venezuela, renews military cooperation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f569e4f888c51128fc638652113c2a513fe75090d0713cb84773345dcce0dd8</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T18:59:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation--c69718d51c80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-hegseth-makes-surprise-trip-to-venezuela-renews-military-cooperation" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth made an unannounced visit to Caracas on Wednesday, announcing a resumption of military cooperation with Venezuela and vowing to crack down on drug traffickers. The trip marks the highest-level US visit since the ouster of Nicolas Maduro in January, signalling a dramatic shift in relations between the two countries.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing has supported Moscow but 'China understands that America is way more important than Russia'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a519af091d54a71d0c572e4be7115b931d4c4adcb8df358d076047d087dab324</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T17:48:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia--f9f88efc8e97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia" /><summary type="html">Following Xi Jinping's very friendly rare tarmac greeting for Donald Trump, Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Kerry Brown, Professor of Chinese Studies and Director of the Lau China Institute at King's College, London. Brown examines the complex relationship between the world's two largest economies, China's growing diplomatic influence and the competition over artificial intelligence.“China is the diplomatic center of the world,” says Brown, pointing to Beijing's ability to bring together leaders from Russia, the United States, Europe and elsewhere. He argues that China now has “extraordinary convening power" and significant influence over Russia.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Democrats nominate Hakeem Jeffries to be first Black speaker of the House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e5a98dfd003f4ff8091f890f16f87e17a9441a0b2205523b9f8d82e4b1579c5</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:44:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house--380c6ed3ece3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-us-democrats-nominate-hakeem-jeffries-to-be-first-black-speaker-of-the-house" /><summary type="html">Democrats nominated Hakeem Jeffries on Wednesday to be the next speaker of the House of Representatives, putting him on track to make history as the nation’s first Black American with the gavel.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Peltola defeats Sullivan in Alaska Senate race, expanding Democratic majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecf636887c0f5e76289aea59380fce64ab6913e47d9e91c28288086393ea1ddf</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T03:47:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-peltola-defeats-sullivan-in-alaska-senate-race-expanding-democratic-majority--a4d690c354ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-peltola-defeats-sullivan-in-alaska-senate-race-expanding-democratic-majority" /><summary type="html">Democrat Mary Peltola defeated Republican Sen. Dan Sullivan in Alaska on Tuesday, completing a political comeback in a state that US President Donald Trump has repeatedly won by wide margins. Her victory gives Democrats a 56-44 Senate majority, marking their biggest net gain in Senate seats since 1958.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Haitians rally behind Bukele as Salvadoran troops battle gangs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bef17d4bb5a7a912e7fb2d123755bdbd36774ae0da44d6737ddeedace39312c7</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T02:42:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-haitians-rally-behind-bukele-as-salvadoran-troops-battle-gangs--576572e0300d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261118-haitians-rally-behind-bukele-as-salvadoran-troops-battle-gangs" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Haitians took to the streets on Tuesday to urge El Salvador's President Nayib Bukele to keep fighting gangs, as his troops bolster security forces in the Caribbean nation. But experts warn that growing public support could turn to anger without a long-term plan to tackle violence and strengthen Haiti's police.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US, Mexico and Bolivia lose measles-free status as deaths mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a3c4ad7aff6e39376edd37b4e29607a9a275e64225dc359c416f733fe6e0c56</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T21:30:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-us-mexico-and-bolivia-lose-measles-free-status-as-deaths-mount--3ecebbb665bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261117-us-mexico-and-bolivia-lose-measles-free-status-as-deaths-mount" /><summary type="html">The US has lost its measles-free status, international health officials said Tuesday, as the highly contagious virus has spread at the fastest rate in more than 30 years, while Mexico and Bolivia also lost their measles-elimination status. Vaccination rates have been falling against a number of diseases, in the US and globally, and measles has been spreading throughout the Americas since 2024.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
